  "summary": "@tekmidian/pai: static keyword co-occurrence in bundled CLI with no traced installer-harm",
  "details": "The package ships a bundled Node CLI under dist/ with multiple minified ESM modules. Static keyword matches fired on co-occurrence of tokens such as `curl`, `ping`, `PATH`, and `Buffer.from(..., 'base64').toString(...)` across several bundle files, and on example-command strings `curl https://example.com` / `curl http://localhost` / `curl http://x` inside a built-in ESLint-rules source file (src/hooks/ts/lib/rules/builtin.generated.ts), which are shaped like rule fixtures / example commands rather than live network calls. No hardcoded attacker C2 endpoint, no browser-credential or wallet-store enumeration, no shell-history or messaging-session collection, no env-var scraping, no credential path reads (~/.aws, ~/.ssh, ~/.npmrc), and no lifecycle script fetch-and-execute pattern was identified. package.json does not declare install/postinstall hooks that fetch remote code. The base64 decode sites are localized to probe/scan helpers without an observed exfiltration sink. The matches are consistent with a general-purpose developer/AI-agent CLI that embeds example shell commands in its own rule set and uses base64 for internal encoding, not with an installer-side attack fingerprint.",
